.TH std::inplace_vector::max_size 3 "2026.11.10" "http://cppreference.com" "C++ Standard Libary"
.SH NAME
std::inplace_vector::max_size \- std::inplace_vector::max_size

.SH Synopsis
static constexpr size_type max_size() noexcept;  (since C++26)

Returns the maximum number of elements the container is able to hold.

.SH Parameters

\fI(none)\fP

.SH Return value

Maximum number of elements, i.e. N.

.SH Complexity

Constant.

.SH Notes

Because each std::inplace_vector<T, N> is a fixed-capacity container, the value returned
by max_size equals N (which is also the value returned by capacity()).

.SH Example


// Run this code

#include <iostream>
#include <locale>
#include <inplace_vector>

int main()
{
    std::inplace_vector<char, 10> p;
    std::inplace_vector<long, 10> q;

    std::cout.imbue(std::locale("en_US.UTF-8"));
    std::cout << std::uppercase
              << "p.max_size() = " << std::dec << p.max_size() << " = 0x"
              << std::hex << p.max_size() << '\\n'
              << "q.max_size() = " << std::dec << q.max_size() << " = 0x"
              << std::hex << q.max_size() << '\\n';
}

.SH Output:

p.max_size() = 10 = 0xA
q.max_size() = 10 = 0xA

.SH See also

size     returns the number of elements
         \fI(public member function)\fP
capacity returns the number of elements that can be held in currently allocated storage
\fB[static]\fP \fI(public static member function)\fP
